WEBVTT

00:00:01.453 --> 00:00:02.745
In the seventh and eighth grade, I

00:00:02.829 --> 00:00:04.956
commuted from Newark to Hoboken via a

00:00:05.039 --> 00:00:06.207
train and two buses.

00:00:06.291 --> 00:00:06.916
And I actually had my

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.668
first business here in Hoboken.

00:00:08.793 --> 00:00:09.919
I was playing my saxophone,

00:00:10.003 --> 00:00:11.337
making money on the train.

00:00:19.387 --> 00:00:21.431
I started my practice a month before the

00:00:21.514 --> 00:00:22.891
coronavirus pandemic.

00:00:23.183 --> 00:00:26.144
My daughter was about seven months old.

00:00:26.227 --> 00:00:27.770
I don't put a ceiling here.

00:00:27.854 --> 00:00:29.063
I'm afraid that this is

00:00:29.147 --> 00:00:30.231
gonna be a cavity that you put.

00:00:30.315 --> 00:00:30.607
I'm gonna put a

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.025
little water on your tooth.

00:00:32.775 --> 00:00:34.444
Never once did I think I can't

00:00:34.527 --> 00:00:36.237
do this or I'm gonna give up.

00:00:36.571 --> 00:00:38.573
I had a lease that I needed to fulfill.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:39.782
I had a dream that I

00:00:39.866 --> 00:00:41.117
was not gonna abandon.

00:00:41.784 --> 00:00:44.329
When the pandemic came, we

00:00:44.412 --> 00:00:46.289
were closed for three months.

00:00:46.498 --> 00:00:48.291
We reopened to a plethora of

00:00:48.374 --> 00:00:50.168
patients, age three to five.

00:00:50.502 --> 00:00:52.003
They needed lots of dental care.

00:00:52.086 --> 00:00:53.755
It was devastating to have to put a

00:00:53.838 --> 00:00:55.590
four-year-old child under general

00:00:55.673 --> 00:00:58.176
anesthesia to fix 16 of their cavities.

00:00:59.052 --> 00:01:02.055
Prevention is way better than fixing the

00:01:02.138 --> 00:01:03.848
problem after it's already occurred.

00:01:04.224 --> 00:01:05.850
And so I thought, where is one place

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:07.560
where children are definitely gonna be?

00:01:07.894 --> 00:01:09.020
Parents are for sure gonna

00:01:09.103 --> 00:01:10.230
send their kids to school.

00:01:10.313 --> 00:01:12.106
So building a school-based program was,

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:14.234
yes, to get these patients, but it was

00:01:14.317 --> 00:01:15.693
really to educate families.

00:01:15.777 --> 00:01:18.863
We started this program in 2022 and we

00:01:18.947 --> 00:01:20.448
started with 16 sites and

00:01:20.532 --> 00:01:21.908
we were local in Newark.

00:01:21.991 --> 00:01:24.494
We've grown to over 70 school locations

00:01:24.577 --> 00:01:26.079
with the most recent location being here

00:01:26.162 --> 00:01:28.623
in Hoboken with the HOPES organization.

00:01:28.748 --> 00:01:29.415
We have been able to

00:01:29.499 --> 00:01:31.292
serve over 3,000 children.

00:01:31.459 --> 00:01:32.502
I think that's kind of

00:01:32.585 --> 00:01:33.670
what I'm most proud about.

00:01:37.006 --> 00:01:37.966
I definitely could not

00:01:38.049 --> 00:01:39.509
do this without my team.

00:01:40.093 --> 00:01:42.971
Once I began getting very busy, I

00:01:43.054 --> 00:01:44.806
couldn't run fast enough.

00:01:45.139 --> 00:01:46.432
It became impossible.

00:01:46.516 --> 00:01:47.850
I had to start delegating.

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:49.102
Don't forget her glasses.

00:01:50.103 --> 00:01:52.772
We had to figure out what could we put

00:01:52.855 --> 00:01:54.399
into our workflow that was gonna make our

00:01:54.482 --> 00:01:56.568
lives a lot easier and that was gonna

00:01:56.651 --> 00:01:58.486
allow us to continue to scale these kids.

00:01:59.821 --> 00:02:00.738
I'm going to school.

00:02:01.155 --> 00:02:02.615
I'm going to school.

00:02:03.783 --> 00:02:05.410
If I was not using

00:02:05.493 --> 00:02:07.495
Lassie, it would be impossible.

00:02:07.579 --> 00:02:08.746
I would come in early

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:09.789
and I would do billing.

00:02:09.956 --> 00:02:10.748
And now I come in a

00:02:10.832 --> 00:02:12.709
little early and I make lattes.

00:02:12.792 --> 00:02:14.502
It does free me up to do more of the

00:02:14.586 --> 00:02:16.671
things that I enjoy, more time with my

00:02:16.754 --> 00:02:18.756
daughter, more time with my partner, more

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:20.466
time with my family, and

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:22.218
more time to continue dreaming.

00:02:23.511 --> 00:02:25.013
I still cannot believe

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:26.556
I'm running a business.

00:02:26.848 --> 00:02:28.057
I'm employing a team.

00:02:28.224 --> 00:02:29.809
We're able to provide a phenomenal

00:02:29.892 --> 00:02:31.019
service to the community.

00:02:31.102 --> 00:02:32.979
That feeling has not changed.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:35.231
What would you say to the kid riding

00:02:35.315 --> 00:02:36.399
those trains across the street?

00:02:37.859 --> 00:02:39.277
Keep playing that saxophone.

00:02:39.485 --> 00:02:41.112
And saxophone today is not

00:02:41.195 --> 00:02:42.405
necessarily an instrument.

00:02:42.739 --> 00:02:43.990
It's a school program.

00:02:44.282 --> 00:02:46.618
A saxophone is my second location.

00:02:47.368 --> 00:02:48.453
Being a public servant in

00:02:48.536 --> 00:02:51.247
my city, it's not a choice.

00:02:51.748 --> 00:02:52.540
It's my calling.

00:02:52.624 --> 00:02:56.169
(Wind Blowing)

